# THE NUMBERS WALK 6b — THE EXAM DOCKET OF CHUKAT, part C: the topic rows of Mishnah Parah (twelve chapters, 96 rows) — the heifer's answer
# sheet; every row read whole from the dump before its verdict.
ROWS = [
 ('Mishnah Parah 1:1', 'DISPUTE', "THE AGE — R. Eliezer: a heifer one year, a cow two; the Sages: the heifer two, the red cow three or four; R. Meir: even five (black hairs feared); ben Azzai's shelashit = three years old. The row heifer_age. Credited (the eighth day's run docket)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 1:2', 'CONTEXT', "the bulls' ages (8:8's second bull) — Beha'alotcha's row, credited."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 1:3', 'CONTEXT', "lambs and rams by age, day to day; the thirteen-month palges — the offerings' rows, credited (three ledgers)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 1:4', 'CONTEXT', "the offerings valid from the thirtieth / the eighth day — the firstling engine's row; context here."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 2:1', 'DISPUTE', "a PREGNANT heifer — R. Eliezer valid, the Sages invalid; bought from gentiles — R. Eliezer no, the Sages yes (Avodah Zarah 23a's row); the omer and the two loaves from the land alone. The rows heifer_pregnant, heifer_from_gentile."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 2:2', 'LAW', "black horns or hoofs chopped off; the eyeball, teeth and tongue do not invalidate; the dwarf valid; an extra digit cut off — R. Yehuda invalid, R. Shimon: where no red hair regrows. CELL heifer_rite('blemish') -> the horn rule; priesthood.blemish by CALL for the consecrated animals' list."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 2:3', 'LAW', "born by caesarean, the harlot's hire, the dog's price invalid (R. Eliezer valid — not brought into the house); ALL BLEMISHES that invalidate consecrated animals invalidate the heifer; riding, leaning, hanging on the tail, crossing a river by it, doubling the rope, a cloak on it invalid; tying, a sandal, a cloak against flies valid — for its own sake valid, for another's invalid. CELL heifer_rite('yoke') -> the general rule; ('blemish') -> the consecrated list."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 2:4', 'LAW', "a bird rested on it valid; a male mounted it invalid (R. Yehuda: made to mount invalid, of itself valid). CELL heifer_rite('yoke') -> the mounting."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 2:5', 'DISPUTE', "TWO BLACK OR WHITE HAIRS in one follicle invalid; R. Yehuda one kos, two adjacent kosot; R. Akiva: four or five dispersed plucked; R. Eliezer even fifty; R. Yehoshua b. Beteira: one on the head and one on the tail invalid; roots and tips — R. Meir by the visible, the Sages by the root. The row heifer_hairs."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:1', 'LAW', "SEVEN DAYS' SEQUESTERING of the burning priest in the Stone Chamber facing north-east; sprinkled all seven days with all the sin-offerings' ashes (R. Yose: the third and seventh only; R. Chanina the deputy: all seven for the heifer, third and seventh for the Day). CELL heifer_rite('sequestering') -> seven days, the sprinklings (Yoma 2a:10)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:2', 'LAW', "the courtyards over rock with a hollow against the grave of the depths; the children born and raised there; the oxen with doors, the stone cups, the Shiloah's water. CELL heifer_rite('procession') -> the children's water."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:3', 'LAW', "the Temple Mount's hollow; the jar of ashes at the courtyard's entrance; the sheep's rope and the stick; the child mixes (R. Yose: no opening for the Sadducees — the child takes and mixes). CELL heifer_rite('procession') -> the ashes taken by the child."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:4', 'DISPUTE', "no sin-offering by virtue of another's preparations; the children sprinkle each other — R. Yose HaGelili; R. Akiva: no need. The row children_sprinkle."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:5', 'DISPUTE', "THE NINE HEIFERS — the residue of the seven used, or six... or one; Moses the first, Ezra the second, five after Ezra (R. Meir) / seven (the Sages): Shimon the Just and Yochanan two each, Elihoenai, Hanamel, Ishmael b. Piabi one each. The row nine_heifers — the shelf's run of the tape's OPEN debit."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:6', 'LAW', "the ramp from the Temple Mount to the Mount of Olives, arches over arches against the grave of the depths — the priest, the heifer and the helpers cross. CELL heifer_rite('outside_the_camp') -> the Mount of Olives by the ramp."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:7', 'LAW', "no black cow and no second red one taken out with it (R. Yose: 'he shall bring HER out' — by herself); the elders first by foot; THE PRIEST DELIBERATELY DEFILED against the Sadducees ('only those on whom the sun has set'). CELL heifer_rite('tvul_yom') -> the burner a tevul yom on purpose; ('taken_out_alone')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:8', 'LAW', "the hands laid, 'my lord high priest, immerse once' — immersed and dried; the pile of cedar, pine, spruce and fig wood as a tower with air holes, its front west. CELL heifer_rite('wood') -> the pile; the immersion."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:9', 'LAW', "bound with a reed rope, head south, face west; the priest east facing west; slaughtered with the right, the blood received in the left (R. Yehuda: right then left); sprinkled with the right, SEVEN DIPS one per sprinkling toward the Holy of Holies; the hand wiped on the body; the fire kindled with chips (R. Akiva: palm branches). CELL heifer_rite('sprinkling') -> each dip its own; ('finger_wipe'); ('slaughter_whole')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:10', 'LAW', "it burst; standing outside its pit he took the cedar, hyssop and scarlet, asking thrice each 'is this cedar?' and answered 'yes' thrice. CELL heifer_rite('kit') -> the threefold question."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 3:11', 'LAW', "wrapped together with the strip's remainder and cast into the fire; beaten with sticks and sifted (R. Yishmael: stone hammers and sieves); a black coal with ashes crushed; a bone crushed either way; THREE PARTS — the rampart, the Mount of Olives, the priestly watches. CELL heifer_rite('kit') -> the bundle cast; ('ashes_thirds') -> three."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 4:1', 'LAW', "slaughtered, received or sprinkled NOT FOR ITS NAME invalid (R. Eliezer valid); unwashed hands or feet invalid (R. Eliezer valid); not by the high priest invalid (R. Yehuda valid); not in all the garments invalid; prepared in WHITE garments. CELL heifer_rite('for_its_name') -> invalid; ('who_burns') -> the high priest (R. Yehuda's arm); ('priest_in_garments') -> white."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 4:2', 'LAW', "burned outside its pit, in two pits, two cows in one pit invalid; the blood not toward the Holy of Holies' entrance invalid; the seventh from the sixth then a seventh invalid; an eighth from the seventh valid. CELL heifer_rite('sprinkling') -> the counting rule; ('outside_the_camp') -> its pit."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 4:3', 'LAW', "burned without wood or with any wood, straw or stubble valid; flayed and cut valid; slaughtered intending to eat its flesh valid (R. Eliezer: no intention invalidates). CELL heifer_rite('wood') -> any; ('for_its_name') -> the eating intention harmless."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 4:4', 'LAW', "ALL OCCUPIED with the heifer beginning to end defile their clothing and invalidate it by other WORK; the invalidity's stringency-turned-leniency; always subject to TRESPASS; wood may be added; BY DAY and BY A PRIEST; work invalidates until it is ashes; work invalidates the water until the ashes are in it. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates'), ('defiles_garments'), ('meilah'), ('day_and_priest')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:1', 'LAW', "the earthen vessel's bringer immerses and sleeps by the furnace (R. Yehuda: from the house too, all trusted for the hatat); for terumah from the second / third row. CELL corpse_tumah('all_trusted') -> the vessel's chain of trust (Tosefta Chagigah 3:20)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:2', 'LAW', "a vessel immersed in water unfit for mixing must be dried; fit, not; to collect already-mixed water, dried either way. CELL corpse_tumah('vessel_for_water') -> the drying rule."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:3', 'LAW', "a pumpkin shell immersed in unfit water — mixing allowed unless it was defiled (R. Yehoshua: beginning and end alike); never to collect mixed water. CELL corpse_tumah('vessel_for_water')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:4', 'DISPUTE', "the reed pipe — R. Eliezer immersed at once, R. Yehoshua defiled then immersed; ALL prepare the mixture except the deaf-mute, imbecile and minor (R. Yehuda: the minor yes, the woman and hermaphrodite no). The row sprinkler_who (Yoma 43a:13's arms)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:5', 'LAW', "the mixture in any vessel — dung, stone, earth, a boat; not in a vessel's walls, a jug's side, a stopper, cupped hands: filling, mixing and sprinkling need a VESSEL; only a vessel's tight cover protects. CELL corpse_tumah('vessel_for_water') -> a vessel required; ('open_vessel')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:6', 'DISPUTE', "a potter's egg fit (R. Yose unfit); a hen's egg — R. Meir and R. Yehuda fit, the Sages unfit. The row vessel_egg."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:7', 'LAW', "a trough in the rock is no vessel — no collecting, mixing, sprinkling, cover or mikveh-invalidation; a movable one joined with lime is; a hole below stopped with a rag invalid, at the side valid; the clay rim. CELL corpse_tumah('vessel_for_water') -> the trough rules."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:8', 'LAW', "two troughs in one stone — mixed in one, the other unprepared unless a spout-sized hole joins them or the water overflows both a garlic-peel deep. CELL corpse_tumah('vessel_for_water')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 5:9', 'LAW', "two stones or troughs set together — the water between unprepared unless joined with lime and movable together. CELL corpse_tumah('vessel_for_water')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 6:1', 'LAW', "THE MIXING — ashes fallen on his hand or the trough's side then in: invalid; from the tube into the trough invalid; taking from the tube then covering it or shutting a door: the ashes valid, the water invalid; put upright on the ground invalid, in his hand valid. CELL corpse_tumah('mixing_order') -> by hand, intentionally (Sukkah 37b). Credited (Naso's exam, the sotah ledger)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 6:2', 'DISPUTE', "ashes floating on the water — R. Meir and R. Shimon: reused for another mixture; the Sages: ashes that touched water never reused; the same at the bottom. The row ashes_reuse."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 6:3', 'LAW', "mixing while a bucket is in the trough: the bucket's water prepared; a sponge in the trough invalidates — empty to the sponge; touching the sponge invalidates. CELL corpse_tumah('mixing_order') -> the sponge."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 6:4', 'LAW', "the water run into a jar over his hand, foot or vegetable leaves invalid; over reed or nut leaves valid: what is susceptible invalidates, what is not does not. CELL corpse_tumah('living_water') -> the susceptible conduit."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 6:5', 'LAW', "a spring diverted into a vat or pools — invalid for zavim, lepers and the hatat: not drawn into a vessel. CELL corpse_tumah('living_water') -> into a vessel (Pesachim 34b)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:1', 'LAW', "five men filled five jars for five mixtures then one, or one then five: all valid; one man's change of mind: only the last / the first valid; 'prepare for yourself' the first, 'for me' all. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the intention's change on the water."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:2', 'LAW', "filling with one hand and working with the other, for himself and another, two jars at once: both invalid — WORK invalidates for oneself or another. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the filling."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:3', 'LAW', "mixing with one hand and working with the other: for himself invalid, for another valid; for both — his invalid, the other's valid; for two at once both valid. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the mixing."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:4', 'LAW', "'prepare for me and I for you' the first valid; 'fill for me and I for you' the latter; 'prepare for me and I draw for you' both valid; 'fill for me and I prepare for you' both invalid. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the four pairings."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:5', 'LAW', "drawing for himself and for the hatat: his own first, fastened, then the hatat's; the hatat's first then his own invalid; his own behind, the hatat's before; both for the hatat one each way. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the order of drawing."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:6', 'LAW', "the rope carried in the usual manner valid, otherwise invalid — the question sent to Yavneh three festivals, ruled valid as a temporary measure. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the rope."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:7', 'LAW', "the rope coiled little by little valid; coiled afterwards invalid (R. Yose: a temporary measure). CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:8', 'LAW', "the jar put away or inverted to draw more: valid; to carry the ashes: invalid; potsherds cleared to hold more valid, to ease pouring invalid. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the purpose test."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:9', 'LAW', "carrying the water and ruling a law, showing the way, killing a snake, picking up food to store: invalid; food to eat, a hindering snake: valid; R. Yehuda's rule — work invalidates whether he stopped or not, non-work only if he stopped. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> R. Yehuda's rule."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:10', 'DISPUTE', "the water handed to an unclean man invalid, to a clean one valid; R. Eliezer: even to an unclean, if the owner did no work. The row water_custody."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:11', 'LAW', "two drawing water, one helping the other raise it or pull a thorn: for one mixture valid, for two invalid (R. Yose: valid by mutual agreement). CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 7:12', 'LAW', "breaking a fence to rebuild it valid, rebuilding invalid; eating figs to store some valid, storing invalid; throwing figs under the tree not to waste them invalid. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:1', 'LAW', "two guarding a trough — one unclean, the water valid in the other's domain; both unclean or both working at once invalid. CELL heifer_rite('work_invalidates') -> the two guards."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:2', 'LAW', "the mixer without sandals (the liquid on the sandal defiles it and it him: 'that which defiled you did not defile me'); on his skin clean; on his garment unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('water_defiles') -> the sandal paradox."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:3', 'LAW', "the burner of the heifer or bulls and the goat's leader DEFILE GARMENTS; the heifer, bulls and goat do not — the garment's paradox. CELL heifer_rite('defiles_garments') -> the burner, not the heifer. Credited (three ledgers)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:4', 'CONTEXT', "the clean bird's carrion in the throat defiles garments, the carrion itself does not — the paradox's third seat (the dietary engine's)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:5', 'CONTEXT', "derived uncleanness defiles liquids not vessels; the liquid then defiles them — the grades' paradox (the clocks engine's degrees)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:6', 'CONTEXT', "an earthenware vessel defiles a liquid, not another vessel — the same paradox."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:7', 'CONTEXT', "what invalidates terumah makes liquid first-grade unclean, except a tevul yom — the grades' row."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:8', 'LAW', "ALL SEAS as a mikveh (R. Meir — 'the gathering of the waters He called seas'); R. Yehuda only the Great Sea; R. Yose: all seas cleanse standing, unfit for zavim, lepers and the hatat water. CELL corpse_tumah('living_water') -> the seas unfit. Credited (three Genesis ledgers)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:9', 'LAW', "spoiled waters unfit (salty, lukewarm); disappointing waters unfit (failing once in seven years; failing in war or drought fit — R. Yehuda unfit). CELL corpse_tumah('living_water') -> the unfit springs."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:10', 'LAW', "the Karmiyon and Pugah unfit (marsh); the Jordan and Yarmuk unfit (mixed: fit and unfit joined; two fit mixed fit — R. Yehuda unfit). CELL corpse_tumah('living_water') -> the rivers (Sanhedrin 5b)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 8:11', 'LAW', "Ahab's well and the Banias cave fit; water changed of itself fit; a distant channel fit if watched (R. Yehuda: presumed); clay fallen in — wait till clear (R. Yishmael) / no need (R. Akiva). CELL corpse_tumah('living_water') -> the fit sources."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:1', 'DISPUTE', "water fallen into the flask — R. Eliezer: sprinkle twice; the Sages: invalid; dew — R. Eliezer: the sun; the Sages: invalid; juice: pour and dry; ink or gum: pour, no drying. The row invalid_water."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:2', 'LAW', "insects fallen in that burst or changed the color invalidate; a beetle always (a tube); a maggot or weevil not (R. Shimon, R. Eliezer b. Yaakov — no moisture). CELL corpse_tumah('invalid_water') -> the insects (Gittin 86b's kartzit)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:3', 'LAW', "a beast or animal drank: invalid; all birds except the dove; creeping things not, except the weasel (Rabban Gamliel: the snake; R. Eliezer: the mouse). CELL corpse_tumah('invalid_water') -> the drinkers."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:4', 'DISPUTE', "intending to drink the hatat water — R. Eliezer invalid, R. Yehoshua when tipped; R. Yose: prepared water — tipped / drunk; poured straight to the throat valid. The row invalid_water."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:5', 'LAW', "invalid hatat water not mixed into mud (a snare; R. Yehuda: neutralized); a cow that drank it — its flesh unclean twenty-four hours (R. Yehuda: neutralized in its bowels). CELL corpse_tumah('invalid_water') -> the cow that drank (the reading's crown)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:6', 'LAW', "hatat water and ashes not carried across a river by ship, floated, or thrown across; crossed with the water to the neck; an empty clean vessel or unprepared water may cross. CELL corpse_tumah('water_transport') -> not by ship."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:7', 'DISPUTE', "valid ashes mixed with wood ashes — the majority for uncleanness, no preparation with them (R. Eliezer: with all). The row ashes_mixed."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:8', 'LAW', "invalidated hatat water defiles one clean for terumah by hands or body, not one clean for the hatat; become unclean, they defile the hatat-clean by hands only. CELL corpse_tumah('water_defiles') -> the two cleannesses."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 9:9', 'LAW', "valid ashes on unfit water — defiles one clean for terumah (the priests' portion), not one clean for the hatat. CELL corpse_tumah('water_defiles')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 10:1', 'DISPUTE', "MADAF — what is susceptible to midras has madaf for the hatat, unclean or clean, a person too; what is susceptible to corpse uncleanness — R. Eliezer no madaf, R. Yehoshua madaf, the Sages: the unclean has it, the clean not. The row madaf."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 10:2', 'LAW', "the hatat-clean who touched a madaf thing is unclean; the flask too; touching food or liquid with the hand unclean, with the foot clean; moved with the hand — R. Yehoshua unclean, the Sages clean. CELL corpse_tumah('madaf') -> the hand."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 10:3', 'LAW', "a jar of hatat water touching a sheretz clean; placed on it — R. Eliezer clean, the Sages unclean; touching food, liquid or Scripture clean; placed on them — R. Yose clean, the Sages unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('madaf') -> placed vs touched."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 10:4', 'LAW', "the hatat-clean touching an oven with the hand unclean, the foot clean; standing on the oven with the flask beyond it, the yoke over the oven — R. Akiva clean, the Sages unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('madaf') -> the oven."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 10:5', 'LAW', "the flask passed over the oven from outside — R. Akiva unclean, the Sages clean; an empty clean vessel or unprepared water may stand over the oven. CELL corpse_tumah('madaf')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 10:6', 'LAW', "a flask of hatat water touching a vessel of holies or terumah: the hatat's unclean, the other clean; both in his hands both unclean; wrapped in papers clean; the hatat's wrapped and the terumah's in hand both unclean; the reverse both clean (R. Yehoshua: the hatat's unclean); on the ground and touched — the hatat's unclean; shifted — R. Yehoshua unclean, the Sages clean. CELL corpse_tumah('madaf') -> the two flasks."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:1', 'LAW', "a flask left uncovered and found covered invalid; covered and found uncovered — invalid if a weasel (Rabban Gamliel: a snake) could drink or dew fall; HATAT WATER NOT PROTECTED BY A TIGHT COVER, unmixed water is. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the hatat water's exception."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:2', 'LAW', "doubtfully pure for terumah is clean for the hatat; 'suspended' for terumah — the hatat water poured out; wooden lattice clean for holies, terumah and the hatat (R. Eliezer: loose wood unclean for the hatat). CELL corpse_tumah('water_defiles') -> the doubt rule."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:3', 'LAW', "pressed figs of terumah fallen into hatat water and eaten — an egg's size: the water unclean and the eater liable to death; less: the water clean, the eater liable (R. Yose: clean figs, clean water); head and most of the body into the water unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('water_defiles') -> the figs."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:4', 'LAW', "all requiring immersion by Torah law defile holies, terumah, common food and second tithe and may not enter the sanctuary; after immersion before sunset: defile holies and invalidate terumah (R. Meir) / invalidate both (the Sages), permitted common and tithe; entering the sanctuary before or after immersion — guilty. CELL corpse_tumah('tevul_yom_hatat') -> the Torah's immersers; ('karet_entry') -> the tevul yom guilty."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:5', 'LAW', "immersers by the scribes' word defile holies and invalidate terumah, permitted common and tithe (the Sages forbid tithe); after immersion permitted all; entering the sanctuary before or after — no guilt. CELL corpse_tumah('tevul_yom_hatat') -> the scribes' immersers."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:6', 'DISPUTE', "all immersers, Torah or scribes, defile hatat water, ashes and the sprinkler by contact or carrying; the susceptible hyssop, unprepared water and an empty clean vessel by contact and carrying (R. Meir) / contact only (the Sages). The row water_defiles."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:7', 'LAW', "HYSSOP with an added name invalid ('this' hyssop valid): lavender, blue, Roman, wild invalid; of unclean terumah invalid, of clean terumah not used but valid; not the young shoots nor the berries; entering the sanctuary after shoots not liable (R. Eliezer: nor berries). CELL corpse_tumah('hyssop_species') -> plain hyssop (metzora's kit by CALL)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:8', 'LAW', "hyssop used for the hatat fit for the leper; gathered for wood and wetted, dried and fit; for food, invalid even dried; for the hatat — as food (R. Meir) / as wood (R. Yehuda, R. Yose, R. Shimon). CELL corpse_tumah('hyssop_species') -> the leper's shared hyssop."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 11:9', 'LAW', "the hyssop's rule: three stalks with three buds (R. Yehuda: three buds per stalk); a growth of three cut apart and bound; cut or bound alone valid; R. Yose: three stalks and buds, the remnants two, the stumps any size. CELL corpse_tumah('hyssop_species') -> three stalks."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:1', 'LAW', "short hyssop lengthened with a thread and spindle-reed; dip, raise, grasp the hyssop and sprinkle (R. Yehuda, R. Shimon: dip with the hyssop itself). CELL corpse_tumah('hyssop_dip') -> lengthened (Sukkah 37a)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:2', 'LAW', "doubt whether the water came from the thread, reed or buds: invalid; two vessels and a doubt: invalid; the needle on the potsherd: invalid; a narrow-mouthed flask dipped the usual way (R. Yehuda: the first sprinkling only); DIMINISHED WATER — the buds' tips dipped, no absorbing; front / behind mistaken invalid, to the sides valid; with or without knowledge; on a hundred vessels. CELL corpse_tumah('hyssop_dip') -> the doubts; ('water_measure') -> the tips."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:3', 'LAW', "intended for the susceptible and sprinkled on the insusceptible — no second sprinkle with the remainder; the reverse — sprinkle again; man and beast likewise; the dripping water valid and defiling. CELL corpse_tumah('sprinkling_on_pure') -> the intention grid (Yoma 14a:5)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:4', 'LAW', "sprinkled from a public window and the water found invalid — the enterer exempt; a private window — liable; THE HIGH PRIEST NEVER LIABLE for entering; the slip before the window: hatat water whose commandment was done does not defile. CELL corpse_tumah('high_priest_exempt') -> the high priest; the window's reliance."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:5', 'LAW', "a clean man holds an unclean axe in his garment's corner and sprinkles on it: clean though the water on it suffices; HOW MUCH WATER — enough to dip the buds' tips and sprinkle (R. Yehuda: as on brass hyssop). CELL corpse_tumah('water_measure') -> the tips (Sifrei 129's elimination); ('sprinkler_carrier')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:6', 'LAW', "unclean hyssop of an egg's size: the water and sprinkling invalid; less: the water valid, the sprinkling invalid; it defiles other hyssop to a hundred. CELL corpse_tumah('water_defiles') -> the hyssop's chain."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:7', 'LAW', "the hatat-clean whose hands became unclean — his body unclean, and his fellow's to a hundred. CELL corpse_tumah('water_defiles') -> the hands' chain."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:8', 'LAW', "a flask unclean outside is unclean inside and defiles another to a hundred; the bell and clapper connected; the spindle stick's parts; the crib's cover; the base not connected; drilled handles connected (R. Yochanan b. Nuri: wedged too). CELL corpse_tumah('connection') -> the connected parts."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:9', 'LAW', "the pack-saddle's baskets, the barrow's bed, the bier's iron corner, travelers' horns, a key chain, the washermen's loose stitches, a garment stitched with kilayim (the forbidden mixture of threads) — connected for uncleanness, not for sprinkling. CELL corpse_tumah('connection') -> not for sprinkling (Shabbat 48b)."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:10', 'LAW', "the kettle's lid on a chain — Beit Shammai: connected for uncleanness not sprinkling; Beit Hillel: sprinkled on the kettle the lid too, not the reverse; ALL SPRINKLE except the tumtum, hermaphrodite, woman and witless child; a woman may assist and hold the water; holding his hand invalid. CELL corpse_tumah('sprinkler_who') -> not a woman; ('connection')."),
 ('Mishnah Parah 12:11', 'LAW', "dipped by day and sprinkled by day valid; dipped by day and sprinkled at night, or the reverse, invalid; he may immerse at night and sprinkle by day — sprinkling from sunrise (from dawn valid). CELL corpse_tumah('sprinkling_day') -> by day (Megillah 20a)."),
]
